# PART 6 – ADVANCED GLASSMORPHISM

Glassmorphism is one of the highest-priority design requirements.

The entire website must use a consistent glassmorphism design language.

## 6.1 Glass Characteristics

Implement:
- Background transparency.
- Backdrop blur.
- Saturation.
- Translucent surfaces.
- Thin luminous borders.
- Soft inner highlights.
- Subtle reflections.
- Layered depth.
- Soft shadows.
- Smooth hover transitions.

Example dark glass:

background: rgba(255,255,255,0.10);

backdrop-filter: blur(24px) saturate(160%);

border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.22);

box-shadow:
0 12px 36px rgba(13,34,61,0.16),
inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,0.24);

Example light glass:

background: rgba(255,255,255,0.58);

backdrop-filter: blur(22px) saturate(155%);

border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.72);

box-shadow:
0 12px 36px rgba(37,69,108,0.10),
inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,0.85);

